   "evidence": "`theorem fromG1G2_ne_zero (\u03b5 ...) (hU : SpinUniquenessAssumptions \u03b5 K) (hM : 0 < K.M2 g) (hpq : g K.p K.q \u2260 0) (h : g\u2081 \u2260 0 \u2228 g\u2082 \u2260 0)` at Tensor.lean:339-341; its own docstring (line 337) correctly reads \"With probe vectors ..., a positive target mass and `p\u00b7q \u2260 0`\". The unpolarized analogue `Tensors.Hadronic.fromF1F2_ne_zero` (Tensors/Basic.lean:706) needs only `hU`, which is presumably where the header wording came from.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Polarized/Tensor.lean",
   "fix": "Move the extra hypotheses before the `fromG1G2_ne_zero` clause, e.g. \"... linearly independent (`linearIndependent_spinStructure`); if moreover `M\u00b2 > 0` and `p\u00b7q \u2260 0`, `fromG1G2` is non-zero unless both values vanish (`fromG1G2_ne_zero`) and determines `g\u2081`, `g\u2082` (`fromG1G2_injective`) ...\".",
   "issue": "The module docstring says that under `SpinUniquenessAssumptions` alone \"`fromG1G2` is non-zero unless both structure-function values vanish (`fromG1G2_ne_zero`); if moreover `M\u00b2 > 0` and `p\u00b7q \u2260 0` ...\". `fromG1G2_ne_zero` (lines 339-341) also requires `hM : 0 < K.M2 g` and `hpq : g K.p K.q \u2260 0`, and it is false without them: at `M\u00b2 \u2264 0`, `\u221a(K.M2 g) = 0` and `fromG1G2 \u03b5 K g\u2081 g\u2082 = 0` for all `g\u2081, g\u2082`.",
